2026-07-31 implementation and debug validation
- Replaced the trivial baseline with a causal DuckDB weekly panel, 209-feature article-origin representation, deterministic fallback bank, forward-fold feature and hyperparameter selection, and global LightGBM L1 models.
- Implemented exact weekly lags, rolling moments, counts, channels, lifecycle, EWMA, trend, price, buyer composition, hierarchy context, seasonality, and lifecycle interactions.
- Implemented Model A train-only validation predictions and Model B train-plus-validation test predictions, clipping, row restoration, debug article subsetting, per-origin Parquet caches, and prediction caches.
- Debug completed in 17.705 seconds and both prediction arrays passed `kapso_datasets/check_predictions.py`.
- Fast evaluator completed with MAE 0.050232985300928165; this official validation result was recorded only after the internal debug design was frozen and was not used for selection.
- Difficulty: the first DuckDB weekly aggregation failed with `Binder Error: No function matches avg(BOOLEAN)` because DuckDB 1.5.4 does not average booleans. Casting all boolean buyer shares to DOUBLE fixed the build.
- Difficulty: the installed LightGBM wheel rejected `device_type=cuda` with `CUDA Tree Learner was not enabled in this build`; its OpenCL `device_type=gpu` path worked and is used for full fits.
- Difficulty: the first full evaluation attempt was terminated after 883.716 seconds because the grader buffered all candidate output and a live 3rd/4th fold was mistaken for one exceptionally slow first fold. The flushed log proved three folds had finished in 130.101, 568.183, and 183.278 seconds; per-fold JSON resume records were added and the original full-panel protocol was retained for retry.
- Difficulty: full evaluation attempt 2 persisted all four demand folds, then crashed with `lightgbm.basic.LightGBMError: bin size 26760 cannot run on GPU` when hierarchy categoricals were introduced. High-cardinality category codes now remain numeric/group-context features, only codes at most 255 are marked categorical on GPU, and a CPU retry handles any remaining GPU-bin rejection; a synthetic high-cardinality fit verified the fix.

2026-07-31 full evaluation and training-only improvement
- Full evaluation attempt 3 completed in 2,435.895 seconds with official validation R2 0.5689550036412203, MAE 0.04345975750905242, and RMSE 0.43482042599980536; the evaluator archived run_0006.
- Training-only gates retained demand features at criterion 0.04391960682786815 and rejected hierarchy 0.04508693236837062 and customer/price widening 0.0446132636341708.
- The predeclared history grid retained 26 origins at 0.04391960682786815 versus 13 origins at 0.04578847474747458 and 52 origins at 0.04463562175157258, freezing 453 trees.
- Reconstructed OOF predictions selected a 50% model and 50% last-week fallback blend at criterion 0.04288394023893059 versus 0.04393958383436686 model-only. The blend improved two folds, reduced variance, was integrated without using official validation labels, and passed prediction checks.

2026-07-31 daily feature widening
- Added a cached DuckDB daily aggregate and 77 causal daily lag, rolling, activity, recency, price, channel, transaction, and distinct-customer features.
- The daily base built in under 3 seconds and one origin feature frame contains 77 float32 columns for 105,542 articles.
- Daily widening improved all four training-only folds to 0.0301528237760067, 0.03487290441989899, 0.04534508287906647, and 0.0352429524064064; criterion improved from 0.04391960682786815 to 0.03960125850081865.
- A repeated fallback blend grid changed the daily criterion by only 0.000006 while worsening mean MAE, so the simpler unblended daily model was retained with 682 frozen rounds.
- Model A and Model B daily fits completed in 236.716 and 224.461 seconds, and both final arrays passed the local contract checker.
- A cross-lane hurdle ensemble was rejected because its training-only criterion improvement was only 0.000084 and required a materially more complex runtime dependency.
